1
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:24,123
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:24,353 --> 00:00:25,810
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:26,885 --> 00:00:32,850
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

4
00:00:34,346 --> 00:00:40,623
During the advances of the army of Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه

5
00:00:40,994 --> 00:00:44,614
we talked about his defeat of Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي).

6
00:00:46,282 --> 00:00:53,991
Saj'jah(سجَّاح) was a woman from the tribe of Taghlub(تغلُب) they were Christians.

7
00:00:54,404 --> 00:00:57,192
 She claimed to be a prophet and she came down from Iraq

8
00:00:58,126 --> 00:01:03,573
and a huge number of followers were surrounding her.

9
00:01:04,554 --> 00:01:09,669
So she came in, joined hands with Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي)

10
00:01:11,127 --> 00:01:13,341
and with Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب) also

11
00:01:14,314 --> 00:01:17,189
and among the people who made a deal with her.

12
00:01:17,881 --> 00:01:23,286
And again, these were political alliances more than they were religious convictions,

13
00:01:23,962 --> 00:01:25,294
was Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة).

14
00:01:26,302 --> 00:01:32,351
Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة) was a Muslim but he refused to pay Zaka'at(زكوة).

15
00:01:33,332 --> 00:01:38,066
And when Saj'jah(سجَّاح) came he made an agreement, a coalition with her.

16
00:01:39,812 --> 00:01:41,442
Now when Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي) was defeated

17
00:01:42,923 --> 00:01:48,083
Saj'jah(سجَّاح) just withdrew, to protect herself.

18
00:01:48,876 --> 00:01:52,814
So, Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة) was now regretting, what he did, he made the wrong move.

19
00:01:53,006 --> 00:01:59,187
He made the deal with this Saj'jah(سجَّاح), false prophet and now he's left alone

20
00:02:00,010 --> 00:02:02,581
and Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه was around the corner.

21
00:02:05,131 --> 00:02:09,464
Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه decided to attack Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة),

22
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:13,162
the Ansaar(أنْصَار) told him: We have done what the Siddique(صديق) told us

23
00:02:14,033 --> 00:02:16,480
and we're not going to join you, so he went ahead,

24
00:02:16,871 --> 00:02:18,396
later on the Ansaar(أنْصَار) said:

25
00:02:18,482 --> 00:02:20,508
He's the Ameer(أمير), let's just follow him.

26
00:02:21,474 --> 00:02:23,246
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), his argument was

27
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:26,281
I cannot wait to get permission from the Khalifah(خليفه)

28
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:30,398
because this is an opportunity that if I Miss, I'm not going to get again.

29
00:02:31,231 --> 00:02:35,906
I have to pounce on demand now, otherwise it will be too late.

30
00:02:37,636 --> 00:02:39,475
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) decided to move ahead

31
00:02:39,714 --> 00:02:42,928
 the Ansaar(أنْصَار) reluctantly agreed and they joined him

32
00:02:42,952 --> 00:02:47,513
and they attacked, they ambushed Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة) and his people.

33
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:52,054
There are two versions of what happened,

34
00:02:52,372 --> 00:02:57,636
One version is that Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه captured Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة)

35
00:02:58,625 --> 00:03:02,780
and discussed the issue of Zaka'at(زكوة) with him and Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة) said:

36
00:03:02,804 --> 00:03:04,649
I will pray but I'm not going to pay Zaka'at(زكوة).

37
00:03:05,177 --> 00:03:07,679
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) ordered his execution.

38
00:03:08,714 --> 00:03:16,631
The other version is that, they were captured and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said;

39
00:03:17,174 --> 00:03:17,951
دَّفِّعُوهُم

40
00:03:18,214 --> 00:03:20,861
Give them warmth because it was a very cold night.

41
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:24,406
And the Arabs had different dialects

42
00:03:24,430 --> 00:03:30,673
I mean it's not that the Arabs in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ all, have the same dialect,

43
00:03:30,794 --> 00:03:32,250
their dialects were different.

44
00:03:34,702 --> 00:03:40,707
And دَّفِّعُوهُم was understood to mean "Kill Them".

45
00:03:43,415 --> 00:03:49,697
So they were executed whichever version was the more accurate one.

46
00:03:50,428 --> 00:03:54,431
Anyway, after that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) married the wife of Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة).

47
00:03:56,286 --> 00:04:03,163
There's a lot of talk that has went around because of the marriage of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to the wife of Malik(مالك)

48
00:04:03,516 --> 00:04:04,911
 and to the killing of Malik(مالك).

49
00:04:05,650 --> 00:04:09,972
Abu Qatada Al-Ansari(أبوقتادةألأنصاري), he immediately just left

50
00:04:10,475 --> 00:04:12,216
and he went to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) and he said;

51
00:04:12,241 --> 00:04:13,853
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) has killed the man

52
00:04:13,916 --> 00:04:18,726
whom I witnessed with my own eyes, making the Adhan(آذَان) and praying,

53
00:04:18,887 --> 00:04:23,101
that his people were making the Adhan(آذَان) and praying and then he takes over his wife.

54
00:04:24,793 --> 00:04:26,457
So this was reported to the Khalifah(خليفه).

55
00:04:27,375 --> 00:04:30,422
 And it’s an incident that's mentioned in At-Tabri(ألطبري) and in the history books.

56
00:04:32,164 --> 00:04:35,376
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was very angry at this.

57
00:04:36,732 --> 00:04:40,354
 And he told Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه that Khalid(خالد) must be fired.

58
00:04:41,179 --> 00:04:44,473
Now again, there's two versions on what happened later

59
00:04:45,219 --> 00:04:47,546
did Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) called Khalid(خالد) or he just sent him a letter.

60
00:04:48,019 --> 00:04:51,892
One version which is mentioned by Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) and At-Tabri(ألطبري) that

61
00:04:52,025 --> 00:04:58,169
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) has called Khalid(خالد) to come to Madina, so that he can investigate the matter.

62
00:04:59,864 --> 00:05:03,243
 So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) comes in to the Masjid An-Nabwi(مسجدألنبوي)

63
00:05:05,348 --> 00:05:13,303
 in his chainmail which is rusty because of the blood that has accumulated on it

64
00:05:14,471 --> 00:05:17,677
and he's wearing his turban and sticking out of it, arrows.

65
00:05:19,149 --> 00:05:21,458
And he comes in to the Masjid An-Nabwi(مسجدألنبوي).

66
00:05:21,483 --> 00:05:25,664
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he sees him, he jumps at him.

67
00:05:26,952 --> 00:05:30,365
He grabs him and he pulls out the arrows from his turban and he says;

68
00:05:30,396 --> 00:05:36,078
You have committed hypocrisy by killing a Muslim and then you take over his wife.

69
00:05:37,903 --> 00:05:42,508
 Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه did not answer back, he was silent and did not say anything.

70
00:05:43,094 --> 00:05:46,983
 Because he thought that maybe this is the view of the Khalifah(خليفه) too and I'm in trouble

71
00:05:47,007 --> 00:05:48,721
so he just stayed quiet.

72
00:05:50,201 --> 00:05:53,667
However, when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه investigated the matter

73
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:59,001
he came to the decision and the verdict that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) is innocent

74
00:05:59,505 --> 00:06:01,929
and that he should carry on in his post

75
00:06:02,413 --> 00:06:10,632
and he told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه I'm not going to sheath a sword that was drawn out by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

76
00:06:14,292 --> 00:06:23,173
Therefore, we would come to the conclusion as many of the historians of Ahlus Sunnah Wal-Jama'ah(أهل السنة والجماعة)

77
00:06:23,739 --> 00:06:26,211
that there was some misunderstanding that happened.

78
00:06:27,234 --> 00:06:31,285
However, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه investigated the matter

79
00:06:31,325 --> 00:06:33,888
and came to the conclusion that whatever happened

80
00:06:34,361 --> 00:06:36,879
 Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) should not be held responsible for it

81
00:06:36,903 --> 00:06:39,324
and he should continue and carry on in his position.

82
00:06:40,343 --> 00:06:43,890
And that Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة) was a man, who was playing

83
00:06:44,898 --> 00:06:49,689
going back and forth, oscillating and he paid the price for his indecisiveness,

84
00:06:50,278 --> 00:06:53,793
in and out of Islam according to the winds of change.

85
00:06:54,742 --> 00:06:58,852
If it appears to be that the Muslims are riding the tide, he becomes a Muslim.

86
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:04,135
If, whenever they go away, he joins in hands with Al-Murtaddeen(ألمرتدين).

87
00:07:04,624 --> 00:07:07,428
And he ended up paying the price for that with his life.

88
00:07:10,573 --> 00:07:13,134
So Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويرة) would be considered as a Murtadd(مُرتَدّ),

89
00:07:13,158 --> 00:07:16,473
because the marriage of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to his wife, carried on

90
00:07:17,055 --> 00:07:21,664
and that could only take place if we would consider him a Murtadd(مُرتَد).

91
00:07:22,801 --> 00:07:26,300
I'm mentioning this because this is one of the events that caused the controversy

92
00:07:26,843 --> 00:07:30,597
around the personality of Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه.

93
00:07:33,010 --> 00:07:37,119
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه), he comments on the issue of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) and

94
00:07:37,679 --> 00:07:40,888
Khalid(خالد) and Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) not particularly this issue, but in general.

95
00:07:41,712 --> 00:07:42,508
He says:

96
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:46,538
وهكذا أبو بكر ما زال يستعمل خالداً في حرب  أهل الردة،

97
00:07:46,919 --> 00:07:52,206
وفي فتوح العراق و الشام، وبدت منه هفوات كان له فيها تأويل

98
00:07:52,277 --> 00:07:59,401
وقد  ذكر له عنه أنه كان له فيها هوى، فلم يعزله من أجلها بل عاتبه عليها؛

99
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:02,666
لرجحان  المصلحة على المفسدة في بقائه،

100
00:08:02,852 --> 00:08:07,276
وأن غيره لم يكن يقوم مقامه؛ لأن المتولي الكبير

101
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:12,546
He says: Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) carried on sending out Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

102
00:08:12,571 --> 00:08:15,908
to lead his armies in the most decisive and important battles.

103
00:08:16,717 --> 00:08:19,330
 Even though it was reported to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق),

104
00:08:19,897 --> 00:08:23,304
that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) has committed some flaws and mistakes

105
00:08:24,027 --> 00:08:27,809
but Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) did not fire him from his post and change him

106
00:08:28,548 --> 00:08:32,131
because the benefit of keeping him was greater than the harm.

107
00:08:33,151 --> 00:08:39,540
And there was nobody who could fulfill the role that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was fulfilling.

108
00:08:40,279 --> 00:08:45,196
There's nobody, who can take that position. And then he says:

109
00:08:46,271 --> 00:08:53,238
لأن المتولي الكبير إذا كان خُلُقه يميل إلى اللين فينبغي أن يكون خُلُق نائبه يميل إلى  الشدة

110
00:08:53,531 --> 00:08:59,827
وإذا كان خلقه يميل إلى الشدة فينبغي أن يكون خلق نائبه يميل إلى اللين؛  ليعتدل الأمر

111
00:09:01,050 --> 00:09:05,828
He said: If the Khalifah(خليفه) has a soft personality

112
00:09:06,918 --> 00:09:11,950
then he should appoint a strong person to be his deputy.

113
00:09:12,884 --> 00:09:18,713
While if the Khalifah(خليفه) has, (I don't want to say strong) because Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was strong

114
00:09:18,737 --> 00:09:22,916
all of them were strong, but was a firm person

115
00:09:23,647 --> 00:09:30,663
 then you'd have to have the deputy being a soft mannered person

116
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:33,768
so that you will have in the end Ietidaal(إعتدال), you'd have a middle way

117
00:09:34,807 --> 00:09:42,154
so he says because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had that flexible and lenient personality,

118
00:09:42,505 --> 00:09:44,559
he appointed Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

119
00:09:44,606 --> 00:09:49,660
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was his deputy

120
00:09:49,993 --> 00:09:51,986
and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was the leader of his armies.

121
00:09:52,576 --> 00:09:56,786
But when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) became Khalifah(خليفه) because of his strong personality.

122
00:09:57,556 --> 00:10:00,221
He changed Khalid(خالد) and he put Abu Obaidah Bin Jarrah(أبوعبيدةبن جراح)

123
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:03,484
who was a very soft man to lead his armies.

124
00:10:04,129 --> 00:10:05,733
And then Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says

125
00:10:06,098 --> 00:10:11,089
and that makes them fulfilled the role of the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Messenger of Allah

126
00:10:11,233 --> 00:10:14,680
because the Messenger of Allah Himself represented the middle way.

127
00:10:16,341 --> 00:10:18,592
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ represented the middle way

128
00:10:18,877 --> 00:10:21,976
he had two deputies Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

129
00:10:22,527 --> 00:10:26,769
One represents one side while the other person represents the opposite side.

130
00:10:27,672 --> 00:10:31,304
But now since Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) have different character

131
00:10:31,485 --> 00:10:33,965
they have to appoint somebody, who represents the opposite

132
00:10:34,202 --> 00:10:41,599
so that they would be similar, the two together combined could be similar to the middle way of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

133
00:10:43,363 --> 00:10:49,116
ليكون أمره معتدلاً ويكون بذالك من خلفاء الرسول صلى الله عليه وسلم

134
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:54,615
الذي هو معتدل حتى قال النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم انا نبي الرحمه انا نبي الملحمه

135
00:10:55,621 --> 00:11:00,510
Rasool Allah ﷺ he himself represents both sides

136
00:11:00,685 --> 00:11:05,159
because Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I am the Prophet of mercy, I am the Prophet of war.

137
00:11:05,357 --> 00:11:08,152
Rasool Ullah said about himself I am the Prophet of mercy

138
00:11:08,692 --> 00:11:11,821
انا نبي الرحمه وانا نبي الملحمه

139
00:11:11,845 --> 00:11:15,886
And I'm the prophet of war, so Rasool Allah ﷺ represents both sides.

140
00:11:18,281 --> 00:11:26,083
 In the Riddah(ردَّة) of Bahrain(بحرين), we know Bahrain(بحرين) today to be the small island in the Persian sea.

141
00:11:26,350 --> 00:11:31,157
But Bahrain(بحرين) in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

142
00:11:32,171 --> 00:11:41,381
used to include Island and other islands of the Persian Sea alongside the eastern coast of Saudi Arabia,

143
00:11:41,889 --> 00:11:44,892
UAE, Qatar, all of that would be called Bahrain(بحرين).

144
00:11:45,677 --> 00:11:49,275
So the entire area was called Bahrain(بحرين) in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

145
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,753
So we'll talk about events that are happening in Bahrain(بحرين).

146
00:11:51,888 --> 00:11:56,208
It includes all of that area Eastern Saudi Arabia and the Gulf states.

147
00:11:58,814 --> 00:12:06,752
Abul Aalaa Al-Hadhrami(أبوالأعلى ألحضرمي) was the head of the Armies fighting the Murtaddeen(مرتدين) in the area of Al-Bahrain(ألبحربن).

148
00:12:07,596 --> 00:12:11,852
A few important events that happened with Abul Aalaa Al-Hadhrami(أبوالأعلى ألحضرمي).

149
00:12:13,169 --> 00:12:19,793
When they set base and chose a camp, something happened, the camels ran away

150
00:12:21,144 --> 00:12:24,559
with the luggage of the soldiers.

151
00:12:25,805 --> 00:12:31,884
And camels have a habit of being aggressive sometimes and untamed

152
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:34,624
so the camels just ran away.

153
00:12:36,052 --> 00:12:44,782
So now the soldiers are left behind without their transport and without their luggage in the middle of nowhere in the desert

154
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:50,942
and there's no water around it's late at night and they're worried.

155
00:12:51,461 --> 00:12:52,361
 What can we do?

156
00:12:52,815 --> 00:12:55,181
Abul Aalaa Al-Hadhrami(أبوالأعلى ألحضرمي) says;

157
00:12:55,905 --> 00:12:57,240
Aren't you Muslims?

158
00:12:58,224 --> 00:13:00,065
Aren't you fighting in the sake of Allah?

159
00:13:01,242 --> 00:13:04,571
Come together and let's ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ let's make Dua(دُعَا).

160
00:13:05,753 --> 00:13:11,014
So he gathered them all and they started making Dua(دُعَا). On and on and on...

161
00:13:11,846 --> 00:13:13,894
And it was the time of Fajr(فجر).

162
00:13:14,615 --> 00:13:21,785
He said: And we started seeing the clouds coming towards our direction and then it poured rain over us

163
00:13:22,406 --> 00:13:24,890
and water started together in pools.

164
00:13:25,985 --> 00:13:31,279
So we drank from that water and then all of our camels came back to drink from that water

165
00:13:31,556 --> 00:13:35,257
and we got our camels back and our luggage and we had water to drink.

166
00:13:36,417 --> 00:13:41,055
Karamah(كرامة) that happened with Abul Aalaa Al-Hadhrami(أبوالأعلى ألحضرمي), this is one.

167
00:13:42,067 --> 00:13:45,453
 Then there's a second Karamah(كرامة) but before that, they attack the enemy.

168
00:13:47,092 --> 00:13:50,995
Actually they attacked the enemy and then pursued them but

169
00:13:52,202 --> 00:13:55,999
 they camped next to the enemy at night.

170
00:13:58,041 --> 00:14:02,526
And then Abul Aalaa(أبوالأعلى) was hearing some loud noise coming from the camp of the enemy.

171
00:14:02,573 --> 00:14:07,410
So he told some of his soldiers to go and spy on them and see what's happening.

172
00:14:07,928 --> 00:14:12,518
So they went and found out that these people are drinking, singing

173
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:15,741
 and that they're so drunk they don't know what they're saying.

174
00:14:16,761 --> 00:14:20,369
Abul Aalaa(أبوالأعلى) said: Get ready! And lets attack them now, middle of the night.

175
00:14:20,857 --> 00:14:24,792
They made their move attacked them, and they were just massacring this army

176
00:14:24,816 --> 00:14:26,699
and they are drunk they don't know what's going on.

177
