359
00:27:58,789 --> 00:28:00,308
أشهد أنَّ محمدًا رسول الله

360
00:28:01,133 --> 00:28:03,147
What do you say about me? He says: I can't hear you.

361
00:28:03,839 --> 00:28:09,618
So Musaylimah(مسيلمة) cuts off part of his body

362
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:14,189
and he asks him again, same answer so it cuts off another part of the body.

363
00:28:14,612 --> 00:28:17,704
and he keeps on cutting him into pieces, until he fell down dead.

364
00:28:18,606 --> 00:28:26,754
So you can see; how evil Musaylimah(مسيلمة) is, that he didn't even stick to the established norms of not killing the messengers

365
00:28:26,809 --> 00:28:31,413
and you can see that Rasool Allah ﷺ even though he had the right to execute these two men

366
00:28:31,450 --> 00:28:33,742
 because of their Riddah(ردَّة), he set them free.

367
00:28:35,207 --> 00:28:40,725
So Habib(حبيب) was a Shaheed(شهيد) in the court of Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب).

368
00:28:41,300 --> 00:28:45,436
There is a very important figure within the movement of Riddah(ردَّة)

369
00:28:45,460 --> 00:28:48,488
his name is Ar-Rajal Bin Unfua Al-Hanfi(ألرجال بن عنفُوة ألحنفي).

370
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:55,707
Ar-Rajal Bin Unfua(ألرجال بن عنفُوة) was part of the delegation that came to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ from Bannu Hanifah(بنوحنيفة).

371
00:28:56,002 --> 00:28:59,443
Bannu Hanifah(بنوحنيفة) just as every other Arab tribe has sent a delegation

372
00:28:59,885 --> 00:29:02,744
paying homage to Rasool Allah ﷺ and giving him Baiyah(بَيْعة) on Islam.

373
00:29:03,498 --> 00:29:06,975
And by the way, Musaylimah(مسيلمة) was a member of this delegation

374
00:29:06,999 --> 00:29:11,079
and he did give Rasool Allah ﷺ Baiyah(بَيْعة) on Islam in one narration.

375
00:29:11,103 --> 00:29:16,718
In another narration, he was actually guarding their belongings and he didn't attend the meeting itself.

376
00:29:17,063 --> 00:29:21,143
But anyway, Bannu Hanifah(بنوحنيفة) were followers of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

377
00:29:21,507 --> 00:29:24,128
So, Ar-Rajal Bin Unfua(ألرجال بن عنفُوة), he stayed behind

378
00:29:24,897 --> 00:29:27,554
and he was attending the Halaqaat(حلقات) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

379
00:29:28,097 --> 00:29:30,907
and he memorized a significant portion of Qur'an.

380
00:29:31,732 --> 00:29:34,647
So, you can say that he had some Ilm(علم) he had some knowledge

381
00:29:35,796 --> 00:29:40,087
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ sent him back to his people to sway them, to bring them back,

382
00:29:40,269 --> 00:29:43,599
 to convince them that what Musaylimah(مسيلمة) is doing is false.

383
00:29:44,579 --> 00:29:49,319
Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) goes there and he turns around 180 degrees

384
00:29:52,846 --> 00:29:54,177
and he becomes a Murtadd(مُرتَد).

385
00:29:55,852 --> 00:30:00,817
And his Fitnah(فِتْنَه) was worse than the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Musaylimah(مسيلمة) himself.

386
00:30:02,094 --> 00:30:06,434
Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه said that I was once in a gathering with Rasool Allah ﷺ

387
00:30:06,458 --> 00:30:10,593
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said that there is a man among you

388
00:30:10,714 --> 00:30:13,777
whose molar tooth in hellfire is bigger than the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

389
00:30:14,922 --> 00:30:19,294
There's somebody sitting with us now, when he dies, he is gonna go to Hell fire

390
00:30:19,318 --> 00:30:23,563
and his molar tooth is bigger than the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

391
00:30:24,082 --> 00:30:29,028
Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) said: Everyone in that gathering died, except me

392
00:30:30,347 --> 00:30:31,499
and Ar-Rajal Bin Unfua(ألرجال بن عنفُوة).

393
00:30:32,321 --> 00:30:34,178
 And I was very frightened because of that.

394
00:30:36,216 --> 00:30:41,069
Until I saw Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) claimed that Musaylimah(مسيلمة) is the messenger of Allah.

395
00:30:41,535 --> 00:30:43,315
 I knew that the Hadith(حديث) is talking about him

396
00:30:45,631 --> 00:30:50,955
because he was worried the only two remaining were him and Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) but then Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) apostated.

397
00:30:51,765 --> 00:30:54,605
 Abu Hurairah(أبوهريرة) says about him;

398
00:30:54,859 --> 00:30:58,932
He was more significant in sowing discord among his people

399
00:30:59,220 --> 00:31:01,161
than was Musaylimah(مسيلمة) himself. Why?

400
00:31:01,338 --> 00:31:02,727
Because of his knowledge.

401
00:31:03,761 --> 00:31:10,397
The Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of somebody, who has knowledge or a scholar is greater than any other Fitnah(فِتْنَه)

402
00:31:11,230 --> 00:31:13,890
 people know that a disbeliever is a disbeliever

403
00:31:14,404 --> 00:31:17,428
but a Munafiq(منافق), who has knowledge is very dangerous.

404
00:31:19,308 --> 00:31:21,498
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث) that

405
00:31:21,775 --> 00:31:25,575
the worst thing I fear for my Ummah(امة) is the hypocrite, who has a very nice tongue

406
00:31:26,450 --> 00:31:28,509
somebody who knows to play around with words.

407
00:31:30,416 --> 00:31:36,128
So when the scholar deviates, an entire people deviate with him

408
00:31:37,179 --> 00:31:43,910
 and that's why when Imam Ahmad Bin Hambal(إمام أحمد بن حنبل) was told by some of his contemporaries

409
00:31:44,881 --> 00:31:53,870
 that in your situation, you're excused you can give in to, what your persecutors want.

410
00:31:54,277 --> 00:32:03,648
 He said: If I speak what they want me to say that would mislead all of the people

411
00:32:04,499 --> 00:32:06,592
 because they wanted him to say that Qur'an is Makhlooq(مخلوق)

412
00:32:06,617 --> 00:32:08,666
 they wanted them to say that Qur'an was created.

413
00:32:09,069 --> 00:32:13,788
He said: If I say that, then the people will go along with me, and he refused.

414
00:32:15,845 --> 00:32:19,298
And that's why the Ahbaar(أحبار) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)

415
00:32:20,107 --> 00:32:23,169
 in the time of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى إبن مريم), when Eesa عليه السّلام gave them Da'wah(دعوة)

416
00:32:23,274 --> 00:32:26,287
 the Ahbaar(أحبار), the scholars of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) when they turned down the Da'wah(دعوة)

417
00:32:26,311 --> 00:32:28,140
the people did not believe in Eesa عليه السّلام.

418
00:32:28,787 --> 00:32:32,644
They said our scholars did not say so, our scholars did not give a fatwa(فتوى) to follow you.

419
00:32:34,246 --> 00:32:35,919
And that's why the people were deceived

420
00:32:36,164 --> 00:32:38,286
and the only people who followed Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى إبن مريم)

421
00:32:38,310 --> 00:32:45,577
were some fishermen and youth but the masses remained behind their deviant scholars.

422
00:32:46,318 --> 00:32:48,493
So it's important to follow the scholars of Haqq(حق)

423
00:32:49,182 --> 00:32:52,750
because it's not just the knowledge that the person possesses.

424
00:32:53,456 --> 00:32:56,578
That is a standard of how close they are to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

425
00:32:57,104 --> 00:32:58,404
Iblees(إبليس) was very scholarly.

426
00:33:00,142 --> 00:33:06,145
And we know of many stories of like Balaam(بلعام) from Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل) and others, who were very scholarly,

427
00:33:07,265 --> 00:33:08,743
 but they refused to accept the truth.

428
00:33:11,083 --> 00:33:16,217
In the time of Musa عليه السّلام when he left his people in the hands of Haroon(هارون)

429
00:33:16,646 --> 00:33:19,059
 because Samri(سامري) was a very charismatic figure

430
00:33:19,657 --> 00:33:23,417
and he knew how to speak well he deceived the people

431
00:33:24,367 --> 00:33:28,133
and he pulled the rug from under Haroon عليه السّلام, who was a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah.

432
00:33:29,444 --> 00:33:33,706
And he took charge over the people and the people left Haroon عليه السّلام and they followed him.

433
00:33:35,455 --> 00:33:38,207
 So it's not always how popular a person is

434
00:33:38,231 --> 00:33:43,493
if you would run Haroon عليه السّلام and As-Samri(ألسامري) in a fair and free elections

435
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:45,121
As-Samri(ألسامري) is gonna win.

436
00:33:46,367 --> 00:33:48,852
So that's not the criteria of how good a person is.

437
00:33:50,094 --> 00:33:54,527
 As-Samri(ألسامري) was deviant and the people followed him, and they left Haroon عليه السّلام. Why?

438
00:33:55,187 --> 00:33:58,161
Because As-Samri(ألسامري), he knew how to fool the people

439
00:33:58,185 --> 00:34:00,847
 and he was a very charismatic figure, himself.

440
00:34:01,773 --> 00:34:03,628
So Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) was a great Fitnah(فِتْنَه)

441
00:34:04,352 --> 00:34:09,520
and in the Battle of Al-Yamamah(أليمامة), Musaylima(مسيلمة) appointed pointed two men

442
00:34:09,993 --> 00:34:13,312
on his right and left flanks, Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) was one of them

443
00:34:13,700 --> 00:34:16,378
and Mahakkam(محكم) was the second.

444
00:34:17,382 --> 00:34:21,520
Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب), even though he was a very bright figure.

445
00:34:22,642 --> 00:34:25,395
When he tried to imitate Qur'an he came up with funny things

446
00:34:25,435 --> 00:34:26,681
and that's Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

447
00:34:27,201 --> 00:34:28,963
 you know, a person can be very eloquent

448
00:34:28,987 --> 00:34:32,557
but when they try to imitate Qur'an they come up with foolish talk.

449
00:34:33,696 --> 00:34:37,268
 He would say, O frog, Croak as you Croak

450
00:34:37,859 --> 00:34:41,047
the bottom of you is in dirt and the top of you is in water.

451
00:34:42,605 --> 00:34:46,228
He would describe this desert rat that has big ears.

452
00:34:46,268 --> 00:34:48,856
He says all of us just head and ears.

453
00:34:49,428 --> 00:34:53,485
Did I mentioned to you about the harvesting Surah(سورة) that he has?

454
00:34:54,938 --> 00:35:02,428
 He says: Planting seeds and then the seeds grow and you harvest the grain

455
00:35:03,466 --> 00:35:08,100
and then you crush it and you make bread out of it and you mix the bread with soup.

456
00:35:10,137 --> 00:35:16,620
والزارعات زرعا،  والمُبذرات زرعًا، والحاصدات حصدًا، والعاجنات عجنًا،

457
00:35:17,565 --> 00:35:21,714
And then he says eat from the Sareed(سريد), the soup with the bread.

458
00:35:22,425 --> 00:35:25,743
Somebody who was listening to this so called Surah(سورة), he said:

459
00:35:25,764 --> 00:35:30,561
O Musaylimah(مسيلمة) I'm not really sure whether your angel is descending

460
00:35:30,582 --> 00:35:34,040
on your heart or on your stomach, it's all about food.

461
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:38,575
And when he heard that Rasool Allah ﷺ was given Al-Kausar(كوثر)

462
00:35:38,609 --> 00:35:40,029
إِنَّا أَعْطَيْنَاكَ الْكَوْثَرَ

463
00:35:40,802 --> 00:35:46,448
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has given Rasool Allah ﷺ Al-Kausar(كوثر), which is a river in Jannah(جنة).

464
00:35:47,431 --> 00:35:48,693
So they told Musaylimah(مسيلمة)

465
00:35:48,717 --> 00:35:51,553
because Musaylimah(مسيلمة) would always try to imitate Rasool Allah ﷺ

466
00:35:52,315 --> 00:35:54,055
because of jealousy, they would tell him,

467
00:35:54,223 --> 00:35:58,126
Rasool Allah ﷺ was given Al-Kausar(كوثر), what were you given? He said:

468
00:35:58,150 --> 00:36:00,540
إنا اعطيناك المفتاح فصلي لربك وارتاح

469
00:36:00,951 --> 00:36:04,988
We have given you the key so pray and rest, he has the key Jannah(جنة).

470
00:36:05,820 --> 00:36:08,139
 It is reported that Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) met him

471
00:36:09,174 --> 00:36:13,237
when Amr Bin Al-Aas رضي الله عنه was a Mushrik(مشرك).

472
00:36:14,593 --> 00:36:19,828
And Amr(عمرو) told him Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has revealed to Muhammadﷺ a Surah(سورة) called Surah Al-Asr(سورة العصر).

473
00:36:20,796 --> 00:36:25,418
So Musaylimah(مسيلمة) said and same thing with me, Allah has given me a Surah(سورة)

474
00:36:25,751 --> 00:36:29,526
يا وَبْر يا وَبْر، إنما أنت أذنان وصَدْر، وسائرك حفز نَقْز

475
00:36:29,920 --> 00:36:32,037
Some of his nonsense. So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said;

476
00:36:32,061 --> 00:36:34,793
والله إنك لتعلم أني أعلم أنك تكذب

477
00:36:35,399 --> 00:36:37,905
In the name of Allah, you know that I know that you're a liar.

478
00:36:39,526 --> 00:36:41,922
 Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), he comments on this and he says

479
00:36:42,195 --> 00:36:49,758
 that the words of Musaylimah(مسيلمة) were so foolish that even a Mushrik(مشرك), a non Muslim realize that his nonsense

480
00:36:49,815 --> 00:36:53,811
 and when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه after the whole fiasco ended

481
00:36:54,487 --> 00:36:59,545
and when he met the delegation of Bannu Hanifa(بنوحنيفه), who came again to give him Baiyah(بَيْعة),

482
00:36:59,886 --> 00:37:02,353
 he said: Can you please tell me some of his Qur'an?

483
00:37:02,769 --> 00:37:06,471
So they said: O Khalifah(خليفه), please excuse us, they know how foolish it was.

484
00:37:06,496 --> 00:37:09,799
 He said: No! I insist on you, to tell me some of the Qur'an of Musaylima(مسيلمة).

485
00:37:09,823 --> 00:37:14,647
So they went ahead, and he said: How could any mind buy into something like this?

486
00:37:16,956 --> 00:37:20,538
To tell you how come they would fall into something like this?

487
00:37:20,570 --> 00:37:26,611
Two reasons, for some people it's like this old man, who came and said,

488
00:37:26,635 --> 00:37:31,126
 I want to meet Musaylima(مسيلمة), they said: Woe to you say, Musaylima(مسيلمة) Rasool Ullah.

489
00:37:31,650 --> 00:37:34,018
 He said: I'm not gonna say that he's Rasool Ullah, until I meet him.

490
00:37:34,471 --> 00:37:38,656
So he goes into meet Musaylima(مسيلمة), and he tells him to narrate some of his Qur'an.

491
00:37:39,145 --> 00:37:43,566
And then the old man says: I know that you are a liar.

492
00:37:44,367 --> 00:37:48,729
But a liar from my tribe is better for me than a true man from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

493
00:37:51,186 --> 00:37:56,274
You are from my tribe, I would rather follow you, then follow Rasool Allah ﷺ

494
00:37:57,012 --> 00:38:00,167
even though that I know that you're a liar and that Muhammadﷺ is telling the truth.

495
00:38:01,742 --> 00:38:05,603
With some other people, it goes back to what Abu Bakr Al-Baqalani(ابوبكرألباقلاني) said;

496
00:38:05,977 --> 00:38:06,906
one of the scholars, he said;

497
00:38:06,930 --> 00:38:13,114
فأما كلام مسيلمة الكذاب وما زعم أنه قرآن فهو أخس من أن ننشغل به وأسخف من أن نفكر فيه

498
00:38:13,525 --> 00:38:16,767
He said: It's so foolish, it doesn't even deserve one to think about it.

499
00:38:17,732 --> 00:38:21,457
وإنما نقلنا منه طرفًا ليتعجب القارئ وليتبصر الناظر

500
00:38:21,820 --> 00:38:25,269
And we only mentioned it to amaze and surprise the reader

501
00:38:26,625 --> 00:38:32,376
فإنه على سخافته قد أضل، وعلى ركاكته قد أزل، وميدان الجهل واسع

502
00:38:32,818 --> 00:38:38,318
And he said: Even though it is so foolish nevertheless, it's still deceived many people

503
00:38:38,674 --> 00:38:40,985
and that's because the field of ignorance is wide.

504
00:38:42,958 --> 00:38:44,060
وكل صاقة كعقدة

505
00:38:44,084 --> 00:38:47,159
For everything that falls down, there will be somebody who will pick it up.

506
00:38:48,914 --> 00:38:53,231
There are going to be people out there, who are going to buy into any cult

507
00:38:54,055 --> 00:38:57,903
whatever idea you throw out there are going to be some people who would buy into it.

508
00:39:00,665 --> 00:39:06,577
Now, not all of Bannu Hanifa(بنوحنيفه) followed Musaylima(مسيلمة).

509
00:39:07,123 --> 00:39:10,945
There were some steadfast among them, like Thumamah Bin Uthaal(ثمامة بن أثال)

510
00:39:11,379 --> 00:39:17,622
he was one of their noble leaders, and he went to his people and he told them

511
00:39:18,282 --> 00:39:22,026
that there is no partnership in Prophethood there's only one prophet

512
00:39:22,397 --> 00:39:26,958
and that's Muhammadﷺ and this man is lying believe and follow me.

513
00:39:27,216 --> 00:39:30,610
Because I am going to go to Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and ask him to give me peace.

514
00:39:32,146 --> 00:39:34,702
And he went to Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Khalid(خالد) granted him peace

515
00:39:34,726 --> 00:39:35,987
and granted his people peace.

516
00:39:36,351 --> 00:39:39,629
And Thumamah(ثمامة) was instrumental in fighting against Al-Murtaddeen(ألمرتدين).

517
00:39:40,118 --> 00:39:44,071
So there were some people from Bannu Hanifa(بنوحنيفه), who did not follow Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب)

518
00:39:44,393 --> 00:39:46,784
among every people, you have good and bad.

519
00:39:48,366 --> 00:39:54,848
So, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was given instructions to attack Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب)

520
00:39:54,911 --> 00:39:58,533
and he was appointed leader among the Muslim armies.

521
00:39:59,233 --> 00:40:04,702
He was entrusted with this very critical event in the time of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

522
00:40:04,726 --> 00:40:10,523
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was so concerned about what was happening in Al-Yamamah(أليمامة)

523
00:40:10,777 --> 00:40:17,253
 that he would go out in the morning waiting for the careers to bring in letters from the combat zone.

524
00:40:17,683 --> 00:40:22,264
Because it was the most dangerous event ever, on Khilafah Al-Islamiya(خِلَافَة ألأإسلامية).

525
00:40:24,776 --> 00:40:32,684
Now, there was a group of about 50 or 60 men from Bannu Hanifa(بنوحنيفه) followers of Musaylimah(مسيلمة),

526
00:40:33,644 --> 00:40:38,419
 who went out to raid another tribe because there was a problem between them

527
00:40:39,088 --> 00:40:41,602
and they were sleeping at night and they didn't know that

528
00:40:41,627 --> 00:40:44,687
they're very close to the camp grounds of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and his army.

529
00:40:46,441 --> 00:40:51,777
So the Muslims succeeded in capturing all of them 50 or 60 men.

530
00:40:54,122 --> 00:40:58,240
So, Khalid(خالد) thought that these were spies.

531
00:40:59,752 --> 00:41:01,207
They said: We're not spies.

532
00:41:01,517 --> 00:41:06,030
We just had this issue with another tribe and we raided them

533
00:41:06,589 --> 00:41:08,966
and we didn't know that you were around and they were telling the truth

534
00:41:09,736 --> 00:41:13,037
Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه knowing that they are followers of Musaylimah(مسيلمة)

535
00:41:13,252 --> 00:41:16,841
ordered the execution of the entire group, 60 men.

536
00:41:19,050 --> 00:41:23,714
The head was Maj'ah(مجاع), he was very respected among his people. So they said;

537
00:41:24,570 --> 00:41:29,587
If you're going to execute us all, spare this man, spare Maj'ah(مجاع),

538
00:41:32,130 --> 00:41:33,126
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) agreed.

539
00:41:33,166 --> 00:41:35,314
He executed all of them and he spared Maj'jah(مجاعة)

540
00:41:35,354 --> 00:41:41,225
and he held him as a hostage with him and he entrusted him to his wife.

541
00:41:42,151 --> 00:41:47,594
The wife of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), the former wife, the ex wife of Malik Bin Nuwaira(مالك بن نويرة) - Umm Tamim(أم تميم).

542
00:41:48,737 --> 00:41:54,545
She was the one, who was entrusted with him obviously, he's in chain.

543
00:41:56,307 --> 00:42:00,384
And this was a setback because he was a very prominent leader among Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة).

544
00:42:00,896 --> 00:42:04,555
 So this was one event that happened before the actual battle, itself.

545
00:42:05,700 --> 00:42:09,395
So now, Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة) mobilized all of their forces

546
00:42:09,954 --> 00:42:13,128
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) mobilize forces,

547
00:42:13,565 --> 00:42:19,813
and they were meeting in this field in Al-Yamamah(أليمامة) and the battle started.

548
00:42:21,569 --> 00:42:27,751
In the first wave of attack, the enemy was so strong in his blow

549
00:42:28,726 --> 00:42:32,983
that it entirely took the Muslims by surprise and push them back.

550
00:42:34,145 --> 00:42:40,447
The wave of attack was so powerful that the A'raab(أعراب), the nomads and the new Muslims

551
00:42:40,661 --> 00:42:43,720
 could not withstand it, and they retreated.

552
00:42:44,208 --> 00:42:51,569
 So now the core group of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) wal-Ansaar(والأنْصَار), are now surrounded

553
00:42:54,771 --> 00:42:56,142
so they had to retreat.

554
00:42:56,736 --> 00:43:02,221
They retreated so much that the spearhead of the enemy

555
00:43:02,245 --> 00:43:04,884
was able to make it to the tent of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) - himself.

556
00:43:04,908 --> 00:43:09,883
Now he wasn't there the tents are set behind the rear of the army.

557
00:43:11,248 --> 00:43:19,281
So the army had to retreat so far, that now the front or the spearhead of the army of Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة)

558
00:43:19,387 --> 00:43:22,988
was able to make it to the actual tent of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

559
00:43:23,641 --> 00:43:26,721
and they came in, and they were about to kill Umm Tamim(أم تميم)

560
00:43:27,905 --> 00:43:33,010
 but Maj'jah(مجَّاعة), who was tied up in the tent, he gave her protection and he said;

561
00:43:33,514 --> 00:43:35,746
This is a great noble woman, Don't touch her.

562
00:43:35,805 --> 00:43:40,718
So it was Maj'jah(مجَّاعة), who protected the wife of Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه.

563
00:43:41,566 --> 00:43:43,481
Obviously then the Muslims had to regroup.

564
00:43:44,445 --> 00:43:47,143
Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) wal-Ansaar(والأنْصَار), they went to Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and said;

565
00:43:47,167 --> 00:43:48,321
يا خالد أخلصنا

566
00:43:48,919 --> 00:43:51,305
O Khalid(خالد) separate us.

567
00:43:52,036 --> 00:43:53,245
What they meant was?

568
00:43:53,421 --> 00:43:56,081
Do not mix us together in this army

569
00:43:56,382 --> 00:43:59,835
have the Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) wal-Ansaar(والأنْصَار) under their own banner.

570
00:44:00,146 --> 00:44:05,019
And these new Muslims and the Bedouins, nomads have them under their own banner

571
00:44:05,043 --> 00:44:08,057
so that we know where we're attacked from.

572
00:44:08,620 --> 00:44:16,519
Because in that initial blow it was the nomads, who retreated and that has caused the entire Muslim army, a setback.

573
00:44:16,876 --> 00:44:17,822
So, now they're saying;

574
00:44:17,954 --> 00:44:19,069
يا خالد أخلصنا

575
00:44:19,253 --> 00:44:20,218
Separator us.

576
00:44:20,409 --> 00:44:21,369
So, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said;

577
00:44:21,444 --> 00:44:26,997
O people organized separately, so that we may know the valor of each clan

578
00:44:27,269 --> 00:44:29,700
and know from where we are approached by the enemy.

579
00:44:29,969 --> 00:44:31,660
Because now there was a blame going on.

580
00:44:32,461 --> 00:44:35,920
 Al Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) wal-Ansaar(والأنْصَار) told the nomads it's because of you this happened

581
00:44:36,510 --> 00:44:39,484
 and the nomads said: No! You settlers don't know, how to fight.?

582
00:44:40,159 --> 00:44:44,344
So they said: Fine, let's all separate under our own banners

583
00:44:44,520 --> 00:44:47,697
so that it will become clear, where we were approached from?

584
00:44:48,575 --> 00:44:52,957
So, now, among A'raab(أعراب) each tribe would be set under their own banners

585
00:44:52,981 --> 00:44:54,346
so you'd know that these are Banu Fulan(بنوفلان).

586
00:44:54,726 --> 00:44:57,180
this is a tribe of so and so, this is a clan of so and so.

587
00:44:57,559 --> 00:45:00,665
And Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) were separate and Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) were separate.

588
00:45:01,310 --> 00:45:06,437
 The leadership of Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) was given to Salim Mola Abu Hudaifah(سالم مولا أبوحذيفة)

589
00:45:06,996 --> 00:45:11,638
and the banner of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار) was given to Thabit Bin Qais(ثابت بن قيس)

590
00:45:12,783 --> 00:45:16,996
Thabit Bin Qais(ثابت بن قيس) is carrying the banner of Ansaar(أنْصَار).

591
00:45:17,021 --> 00:45:23,482
And now it's going to be shame for any battalion to be defeated.

592
00:45:25,229 --> 00:45:27,397
So they have to show their steadfastness.

593
00:45:27,675 --> 00:45:28,926
So what Thabit(ثابت) did

594
00:45:29,271 --> 00:45:32,982
he made for himself a hole in the ground that buried him, a knee high.

595
00:45:34,638 --> 00:45:36,901
So, that he cannot retreat even if he wanted to

596
00:45:37,666 --> 00:45:41,625
and he held the banner and he fought, until he was killed.

597
00:45:42,303 --> 00:45:48,836
Salim(سالم), who was a servant and this shows you equality in Islam.

598
00:45:49,504 --> 00:45:54,048
Among Al-Muhajireen(مهاجرين), you've people from every different tribe and groups

599
00:45:54,441 --> 00:45:58,988
but they have given their banner to Salim(سالم) who was a slave. Why?

600
00:45:59,013 --> 00:46:02,351
Because he was Hamil-Al Qur'an(حاما ألقرآن) because he was a memorizer of Qur'an

601
00:46:03,026 --> 00:46:05,306
 and he said: I know why you give me the banner?

602
00:46:05,652 --> 00:46:07,125
It's because of the Qur'an.

603
00:46:07,877 --> 00:46:08,303
And he said:

604
00:46:08,424 --> 00:46:11,825
بِئس حامل القرآن أنا أن أوتيتم من قِبَلِ

605
00:46:12,142 --> 00:46:16,838
He said: I'm the worst carrier of Qur'an, if you will be approached from my side.

606
00:46:18,202 --> 00:46:23,078
 It's not appropriate for somebody, who's carrying Qur'an to do something against Qur'an.

607
00:46:23,558 --> 00:46:28,149
Qur'an is not just memorizing it, in your heart, Qur'an is applying it to your life.

608
00:46:28,427 --> 00:46:29,889
That's the understanding of the Sahabah(صحابه).

609
00:46:30,276 --> 00:46:33,653
If you are memorizing Qur'an, you have to live up to a certain standard

610
00:46:34,977 --> 00:46:39,527
because you have Qur'an in your chest, you have to follow what you know.

611
00:46:40,649 --> 00:46:43,665
Practice what you preach and walk the talk.

612
00:46:44,231 --> 00:46:48,199
Not just memorize it, so that Qur'an can be Hujjah Alaik(حجة عليك) on the day of judgment

613
00:46:48,223 --> 00:46:50,205
 it can be evidence against you on the Day of Judgment.

614
00:46:52,530 --> 00:46:56,169
So Salim(سالم) carried the banner and he fought and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) were firm

615
00:46:56,193 --> 00:46:57,555
and the Ansaar(أنْصَار) were firm.

616
00:46:58,411 --> 00:47:01,722
But Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة) were putting up a stiff resistance

617
00:47:02,164 --> 00:47:04,662
and the attack was going on in waves.

618
00:47:05,052 --> 00:47:08,968
A wave would attack and then they would go back and another wave would come

619
00:47:09,574 --> 00:47:11,828
and those waves were going both ways

620
00:47:13,011 --> 00:47:16,946
The Muslims were sending out waves and the Mushrikeen(مُشركين) were sending out waves.

621
00:47:17,911 --> 00:47:19,864
 And the Muslims had to encourage each other

622
00:47:20,337 --> 00:47:22,737
and they would have speakers stand up and give Mu'aza(مؤعظة)

623
00:47:22,761 --> 00:47:24,665
and give a Khut'ba(خطبة) to encourage others to fight.

624
00:47:25,333 --> 00:47:28,677
So Zaid Ibn Al-Khattab(زيد إبن الخطاب), the brother of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he told

625
00:47:28,939 --> 00:47:35,231
 his followers grit your teeth, meaning press your nerves very hard and just attack

626
00:47:36,880 --> 00:47:41,391
go straight ahead, grit your teeth people and Strike your enemy and proceed straight ahead.

627
00:47:42,388 --> 00:47:46,538
And they made a very powerful and violent blow to the enemy

628
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:49,836
and Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) was killed,

629
00:47:50,485 --> 00:47:55,089
Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) the second in command after Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب) was killed.

630
00:47:55,421 --> 00:47:58,716
And the one, who killed him was Zaid Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

631
00:48:00,049 --> 00:48:03,445
Abdur Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr(عبدالرحمن إبن أبي بكر) he saw Al-Muhakkam(ألمحكم)

632
00:48:03,469 --> 00:48:08,351
which is also the head of the other flank of the army of Musaylimah(مسيلمة)

633
00:48:08,375 --> 00:48:12,528
you had Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) and Al-Muhakkam(ألمحكم) they were the right and left flank.

634
00:48:13,282 --> 00:48:15,896
So Abdur Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr(عبدالرحمن إبن أبي بكر) spoted Al-Muhakkam(ألمحكم)

635
00:48:16,314 --> 00:48:19,734
giving a speech to his people encouraging them to fight.

636
00:48:20,707 --> 00:48:24,699
And I mentioned to you that Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was a very good Archer.

637
00:48:25,899 --> 00:48:30,943
So he was able to strike Al-Muhakkam(ألمحكم) right in his throat,

638
00:48:31,009 --> 00:48:33,611
while he was standing and giving a speech and he dropped him dead.

639
00:48:34,641 --> 00:48:38,148
So now you have Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) and Al-Muhakkam(ألمحكم) are both dead

640
00:48:38,904 --> 00:48:41,299
but still Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة) were fighting.

